> # 2026-08-08: hw-go and hw-python ship an immutable shell PID-1 entrypoint
> # (`sh -c /hw-go`, `sh -c run-hw-python.py`) baked into their images, which
> # tripped ZTX-A1 as a CRITICAL false positive on every pod start. This exempts
> # ONLY the container's PID-1 process running that EXACT command line - mirroring
> # the existing ztx_declared_python_xapp_entrypoint / ztx_kpimon_go_own_binaries
> # exemptions. An attacker-spawned shell runs as a non-PID-1 child with a
> # different cmdline and therefore still matches ZTX-A1 and is still flagged.
> - macro: ztx_declared_shell_entrypoint
>   condition: >
>     (proc.vpid=1 and
>      ((container.name=hw-go and proc.cmdline="sh -c /hw-go") or
>       (container.name=hw-python and proc.cmdline="sh -c run-hw-python.py")))
> 
